{
  "$comment": [
    "The field taxonomy, in one place because two runtimes need it: the",
    "generation pass in Python, which offers the leaves to the model, and the",
    "reader in TypeScript, which groups them for display. Kept as data rather",
    "than duplicated as code, because a story's field would otherwise depend on",
    "which copy was edited last.",
    "",
    "Stories are tagged with a LEAF. Groups exist only for presentation, so",
    "regrouping -- promoting mathematics to the top level once there is enough",
    "of it, merging AI back into computer science -- is a change to this file",
    "with no re-tagging and no migration. That is the whole point of storing the",
    "finer thing.",
    "",
    "The leaves were derived from a tagging pass over 150 stories drawn at",
    "random from the corpus, which named each story's field in its own words",
    "before seeing any candidate list. Names that appeared there and had nowhere",
    "to go became leaves; leaves nothing filled were cut. See",
    "docs/v2/FIELDS.md."
  ],
